{%- comment -%}
  Reviews, rendered by us from Loox's Storefront API.

  Loox's own section draws its reviews inside a cross-origin iframe, so neither
  its markup nor its review text is reachable from the theme - not by CSS and
  not by Liquid. The Storefront API lifts that ceiling: it returns the review
  bodies, media, replies and the rating distribution as JSON, keyed by Shopify
  product id, with no key in the page (it authenticates by CORS origin, so only
  calls from the store's own domain are accepted). The cards below are therefore
  ours to design.

  The section renders BOTH of these, and they work independently:

  - Inline, as a band in the page, under the "What buyers say" heading. Its
    list is fetched when the band nears the viewport.
  - As a popup, opened from the rating row in the buy box
    (snippets/product-info.liquid). The dialog is fixed and hidden until the
    row is clicked, and its list is fetched on the first open.

  Each is its own instance of the panel (snippets/pdp-reviews-panel), its own
  lightbox (snippets/pdp-reviews-lightbox) and its own [data-pdp-reviews]
  root, so pdp-reviews.js runs once per instance and neither knows about the
  other. The bottomline call (average, count, distribution) is cached in the
  script, so the two instances share one request for it.

  Two things stay deliberate:

  - The whole list is client-rendered, so review text is not in the server HTML
    and earns no rich-snippet value. The rating row is what Google reads from
    this page, and it comes from product.metafields.loox via Loox's own JSON-LD.
  - Nothing renders until the store's Loox public store ID is set. Loox's own
    app section has been removed from templates/product.json, so without the
    id this page has no review list at all - hence the notice below, which
    shows in the theme editor only. The buy box's rating row is unaffected
    either way: it still falls back to scraping Loox's loox-rating block
    (which stays in the main-product section) when the API has not answered.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    One ID for the whole store, held in a metaobject rather than a theme
    setting so it belongs to the store, not to whichever theme is published,
    and so it is editable in the admin under Content -> Metaobjects. The
    definition is type "loox" with a single-line text field "public_store_id";
    the store keeps one entry of it, and that entry is what is read here. Every
    product page reads it from here; there is no per-section override.
  endcomment
  assign loox_entry = shop.metaobjects.loox.values | first
  assign store_id = loox_entry.public_store_id.value | strip
  if store_id == blank
    assign store_id = settings.loox_public_store_id | strip
  endif
  if store_id == blank
    assign store_id = section.settings.public_store_id | strip
  endif
  assign live = false
  if store_id != blank and product != blank
    assign live = true
  endif
  assign slider = true
  if section.settings.layout == 'grid'
    assign slider = false
  endif
-%}

{{ 'pdp-reviews.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- if live -%}
  {%- if slider -%}
    <script src="{{ 'cau-drag-scroll.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
  {%- endif -%}
  <script src="{{ 'pdp-reviews.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}

<section class="pdp-reviews{% if live %} pdp-reviews--live{% endif %}" id="reviews">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="pdp-reviews__head">
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="pdp-reviews__title">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        No rating row here. It would restate the score block immediately below
        it, which carries the same average, the same stars and a fuller count.
        The buy box keeps its own row (product-info.liquid) - that one is far
        from this panel and still earns its place, and CAU.setRating fills it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
    </div>

    {%- if live == false and request.design_mode -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Editor only. On the storefront an unconfigured section stays quiet -
        a heading with nothing under it - rather than showing shoppers a
        message meant for whoever is setting the section up.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="pdp-reviews__setup">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 8h.01M11 12h1v4h1"/></svg>
        <span>Add an entry to the <b>loox</b> metaobject under <b>Content &rarr; Metaobjects</b> with your Loox <b>public store ID</b> in its <b>public_store_id</b> field to show reviews here. Find the ID in the Loox admin under Settings &rarr; API Keys.</span>
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if live -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The inline instance. Everything inside is filled by pdp-reviews.js. It
        ships empty, and the placeholder cards appear only once a request is
        actually in flight - never from page load. The list is fetched when
        this wrapper nears the viewport, which on a page this long is usually
        well after paint, and a skeleton sitting there through all of that
        reads as a page that never loaded. Once a request is out, though, the
        placeholders are what stop the rail collapsing and springing back as
        the answer lands.

        The slider class sits on this wrapper, not the section, so the rail
        styling reaches the inline list and not the popup's grid.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div
        class="pdp-reviews__inline{% if slider %} pdp-reviews--slider{% endif %}"
        data-pdp-reviews
        data-store="{{ store_id | escape }}"
        data-product="{{ product.id }}"
        data-per-page="{{ section.settings.per_page | default: 4 }}"
        data-sort="{{ section.settings.sort | default: 'featured' }}"
        data-layout="{% if slider %}slider{% else %}grid{% endif %}"
      >
        {%- render 'pdp-reviews-panel', section: section, slider: slider, is_modal: false -%}
        {%- render 'pdp-reviews-lightbox' -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if live -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The popup instance. Fixed, hidden, and outside the .container - it is
      not part of the page's flow at all. The trigger is the rating row in the
      buy box (snippets/product-info.liquid), which the JS upgrades from its
      anchor fallback once this dialog is on the page.

      Opening is what loads the list: the IntersectionObserver that defers the
      inline fetch has nothing to watch here, so the script fetches on the
      first open instead. Always a grid - the dialog scrolls vertically and a
      rail inside it would fight that.

      The wrapper is the JS root; the dialog and the lightbox are siblings in
      it rather than nested, because the dialog's backdrop blur would otherwise
      trap the fixed lightbox inside its own stacking context.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div
      class="pdp-reviews__popup"
      data-pdp-reviews
      data-store="{{ store_id | escape }}"
      data-product="{{ product.id }}"
      data-per-page="{{ section.settings.per_page | default: 6 }}"
      data-sort="{{ section.settings.sort | default: 'featured' }}"
      data-layout="grid"
    >
      <div class="revmodal" data-pdp-reviews-modal hidden>
        <div class="revmodal__panel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
             aria-labelledby="revmodal-title-{{ section.id }}">
          <div class="revmodal__head">
            <h2 class="revmodal__title" id="revmodal-title-{{ section.id }}">
              {{- section.settings.heading | default: 'Reviews' | escape -}}
            </h2>
            <button type="button" class="revmodal__close" data-pdp-reviews-modal-close aria-label="Close reviews">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"/></svg>
            </button>
          </div>

          <div class="revmodal__body">
            {%- render 'pdp-reviews-panel', section: section, slider: false, is_modal: true -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      {%- render 'pdp-reviews-lightbox' -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Reviews",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "shopify-section--pdp-reviews",
  "enabled_on": { "templates": ["product"] },
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "What buyers say" },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Loox Storefront API"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Reviews are rendered here from the Loox Storefront API, in the theme's own design, both as this inline section and as a popup opened from the rating row in the buy box. The store ID is read from the loox metaobject entry under Content → Metaobjects, or Theme settings → Product page (CoppedAU) → Reviews."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "Layout",
      "default": "slider",
      "options": [
        { "value": "slider", "label": "Slider" },
        { "value": "grid", "label": "Grid (Prototype)" }
      ],
      "info": "The slider is a horizontal rail that pulls in the next page as you reach the end; the grid is a 2-column layout with a Load more button."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "sort",
      "label": "Default sort",
      "default": "featured",
      "options": [
        { "value": "featured", "label": "Featured (pinned, then photo and video)" },
        { "value": "date", "label": "Most recent" },
        { "value": "rating", "label": "Highest rated" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "per_page",
      "label": "Reviews per page",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 24,
      "step": 2,
      "default": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_distribution",
      "label": "Show rating breakdown in popup",
      "default": true
    }
  ],
  "presets": [ { "name": "Reviews" } ]
}
{% endschema %}
